## Important behaviors

- **Don't over-engineer.** This is an evaluation harness, not production code. Single-pass through, results saved, move on. No fancy class hierarchies, no abstract base classes, just working notebooks.
- **Prompt for API keys at runtime** when needed using `getpass.getpass()`. Don't ask me for them upfront — only when each notebook actually needs them.
- **Fail gracefully.** If a model can't load (missing dependency, OOM, API error), log it and continue with remaining alternatives. Don't crash the whole notebook.
- **Cache aggressively.** If a model has already produced output, skip re-running it unless I explicitly request a refresh. Stem separation and ASR are slow; don't redo work.
- **Document time spent per cell.** Time each model run so I know which are fast vs. slow.
- **Listening cells matter.** For audio components, include `IPython.display.Audio` cells so I can listen to outputs inline. For video, save and provide path.
- **Tell me when you're stuck.** If a model needs setup that's beyond reasonable (compiling from source, paid-only API access I don't have), document it and skip rather than spending hours debugging.
- **Sanity-check before going deep.** Before building all 8 notebooks, confirm your overall plan with me — directory structure, model selection per component, metric choices. I'd rather sanity-check for 10 minutes than have you build in a wrong direction for hours.

